############################################################
# DIAGNOSIS — verification blocked by HOST CPU starvation (not an app fault)
############################################################
# AUTHORITATIVE evidence = container termination reason (NOT node pressure):
#   lastState.terminated.Reason = "Error"(exit 137) / "Completed"(exit 0) on every restart, and
#   NEVER "OOMKilled". A cgroup memory-limit OOM would report Reason=OOMKilled even with node
#   MemoryPressure=False (it's a per-container cgroup kill, not node eviction) — so node pressure
#   is the WRONG signal to rule out OOM. exit 0 = graceful SIGTERM drain; exit 137 = SIGKILL after
#   a liveness-kill didn't finish draining in the grace window.
#   (For reference only: node MemoryPressure/DiskPressure were also False.)
# => kubelet is restarting pods because /healthz/liveness probes time out while the Docker
#    Desktop VM is CPU-saturated (cold from-scratch start of 3-node kind + Calico + full
#    Prometheus/Grafana + KEDA + metrics-server + app + PG + Redis on one laptop). The app
#    shuts down CLEANLY each time (exit 0) — it is not crashing.
#
# CONCLUSION:
#   - from-scratch BUILD: PASS (make all exit 0; all pods reached Running).
#   - functional/security behaviour on identical 0.1.5: PASS earlier this session
#     (logs/S-metrics-port-split.log, logs/S-ioc-audit.log, M2/M6 smoke) when the host had
#     headroom. The from-scratch RE-verify is environment-limited, not code-limited.
#
# RECOMMENDATIONS (host capacity):
#   1. Increase Docker Desktop CPU/RAM (Settings -> Resources) before the demo.
#   2. Spin up ~10 min before the call and let it settle; do NOT run `make all` live.
#   3. Robustness finding [APPLIED]: probes had no timeoutSeconds (defaults to 1s). Under a
#      briefly-starved event loop that trips a needless restart. Added timeoutSeconds (startup 3,
#      liveness 5, readiness 3) + startup failureThreshold 30->45 in 40-iocheck.yaml so probes
#      tolerate transient slowness while still catching a genuinely dead process. Manifest-only
#      (image stays 0.1.5); takes effect on next `make all`/deploy.
